Q=[
make(1,"The science room ___ quiet before the experiment. Which word completes the sentence?",{"A":"is","B":"are","C":"am","D":"be"},"A","The subject the science room is singular, so the present form of be is is.","Find the subject number first, then match it with the present form of be.",["Locate the subject: the science room.","Recognize that room is singular.","Compare singular present forms of be.","Remove are, am, and the base form be.","Choose A and read the complete sentence aloud."],"easy"),
make(2,"___ two extra chairs beside the window for visitors.",{"A":"There is","B":"There are","C":"It are","D":"They is"},"B","The noun two extra chairs is plural, so the existential pattern is There are.","Use the noun after the blank, not the nearby location, to choose the number of the existential verb.",["Read the noun phrase after the blank.","Notice that two chairs is plural.","Match a plural noun with There are.","Reject There is and the ungrammatical pronoun forms.","Select B and check the full classroom statement."],"easy"),
make(3,"Nina ___ her vocabulary notebook every morning before class.",{"A":"check","B":"checks","C":"checking","D":"checked"},"B","Nina is a third-person singular subject and every morning signals a habitual present action, so checks is correct.","Combine the time expression with the subject form before selecting the verb ending.",["Circle every morning as a habit clue.","Identify Nina as third-person singular.","Use the simple present for a habit.","Add -s to check for this subject.","Choose B and verify the sentence describes a routine."],"easy"),
make(4,"Look! The students ___ a model bridge in the technology classroom.",{"A":"build","B":"built","C":"are building","D":"will build"},"C","Look! describes an action happening now, so the present progressive are building is required for plural students.","Use the immediate-time signal and then match the auxiliary and -ing form to the plural subject.",["Find Look! as the immediate-action clue.","Identify students as a plural subject.","Form the present progressive with are plus building.","Reject the habitual, past, and future alternatives.","Select C and reread the sentence with the ongoing action."],"medium"),
make(5,"Yesterday, our class ___ at the museum until noon.",{"A":"is","B":"are","C":"was","D":"be"},"C","Yesterday places the event in the past, and our class is treated as a singular group noun here, so was fits.","Read the past-time marker, then check whether the subject takes the singular past form of be.",["Locate yesterday as the past-time signal.","Identify our class as a singular group noun.","Choose the singular past form of be.","Eliminate present forms and the base form.","Select C and check the time and subject agreement."],"medium"),
make(6,"A careful student ___ use the lab computer without permission.",{"A":"can","B":"can to","C":"cans to","D":"is can"},"A","A modal is followed by the base verb: can use; the other forms break that pattern.","After a modal, check that the next verb is the base form without to or an -s ending.",["Identify the modal meaning ability or permission: can.","Look at the verb that follows: use.","Confirm that can takes the base form without to.","Remove can to, cans to, and is can.","Choose A and read can use as one verb phrase."],"easy"),
make(7,"___ did you put the attendance sheet? — On the teacher's desk.",{"A":"Where","B":"When","C":"Why","D":"Who"},"A","The answer names a place, so the question word asking for a location is Where.","Use the information in the answer to identify what the question must ask for.",["Read the answer: on the teacher's desk.","Classify that information as a place.","Match a place with Where.","Reject When, Why, and Who because they ask for time, reason, and person.","Select A and check the question-answer pair."],"easy"),
make(8,"This map is ___ than the old one, so new students can read it more easily.",{"A":"clear","B":"clearer","C":"clearest","D":"more clear than"},"B","The sentence compares two maps and uses than, so the comparative form clearer than is correct.","Look for than and the two-item comparison before choosing the adjective form.",["Find the comparison marker than.","Identify the two items: this map and the old one.","Form the comparative of the short adjective clear.","Reject the superlative and the incomplete or less natural alternatives.","Choose B and confirm clearer than expresses the comparison."],"medium"),
make(9,"We stayed inside ___ the rain was very heavy.",{"A":"but","B":"because","C":"or","D":"so"},"B","The second clause gives the reason for staying inside, so because correctly links the action and its cause.","Identify the logical relationship between the two clauses rather than choosing a connector by position.",["Identify the result: we stayed inside.","Identify the explanation: the rain was very heavy.","Match an explanation with because.","Reject contrast, choice, and result connectors.","Select B and reread the cause-and-action relationship."],"medium"),
make(10,"The class has finished the poster plan. They ___ present it at the school fair next Friday.",{"A":"are going to","B":"went to","C":"going","D":"are go to"},"A","A completed plan for a future event is expressed with be going to plus the base verb present.","Use the planned future clue and check the full be going to structure.",["Find the future time clue next Friday.","Notice that the class already has a plan.","Form be going to with plural subject they: are going to.","Add the base verb present after the structure.","Choose A and verify the planned-future meaning."],"hard"),
]
